fb4d9cdf76f264dd0f01f0d6adeabef3/1751259439/hls_264_master.m3u8?t=1447358492","mp4":"https://cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com/steam/apps/2029063/movie480.mp4"}],"genres":["Action","Adventure","Indie"],"features":["Single-player","Multi-player","Steam Achievements","Steam Cloud","Remote Play on TV","Steam Trading Cards","Family Sharing"],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":true,"linux":true},"controller":"full","dev":["Drinkbox Studios"],"pub":["Drinkbox Studios","Kepler Ghost"],"released":"Aug 8, 2013","meta":88,"langs":["English","French","Italian","German","Portuguese - Brazil","Spanish - Latin America"],"min":[["OS","Windows 7, 8, XP, 2000 and Vista"],["Processor","2 Ghz+"],["Memory","512 MB RAM"],["Graphics","Shader Model 3.0, 256 MB VRAM"],["DirectX","Version 9.0c"],["Storage","800 MB available space"],["Additional Notes","Supports Xbox 360 Controller and other XInput-compatible controllers"]],"rec":[],"deck":3,"blurb":"Wrestling moves double as both weapons and keys in Guacamelee! Gold Edition, an exploration-driven platformer in the Metroidvania mold, set in a world drawn from Mexican culture and folklore. The hero is a luchador, and moves such as the Rooster Uppercut serve in combat and also for reaching new places, so fighting and platforming feed into each other. A dimension-swap mechanic shifts the world between two states, revealing hidden areas that are otherwise unreachable.\n\nA second player can join in local co-op, and the Gold Edition is a fuller release of the game. It suits fans of Metroidvanias and melee brawlers who enjoy colorful, folklore-inspired settings and are happy to backtrack as new abilities unlock."}}